📊 Business Intelligence Research Dashboard – Excel

 📌 Project Overview

The Business Intelligence Research Dashboard is an interactive Excel-based data analysis project that analyzes research studies related to workplace diversity, business impact, industries, countries/regions, and research focus areas.
The project transforms a structured research dataset into meaningful insights using Excel data cleaning, PivotTables, charts, KPIs, and an interactive dashboard.
The dashboard provides a consolidated view of the research landscape and helps users understand trends across industries, regions, research topics, and business outcomes.

🎯 Objective

The main objectives of this project are to:

* Analyze research studies related to workplace diversity and inclusion.
* Understand how research is distributed across different industries and countries/regions.
* Identify major research focus areas.
* Analyze the business impact highlighted in different studies.
* Identify trends in research activity over the years.
* Build an interactive and easy-to-understand Excel dashboard.
* Convert raw research data into meaningful business insights.

📂 Dataset

The dataset contains 20 research studies collected from published research and reports.

Dataset contains the following fields:

| Column          | Description                                             |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Study ID        | Unique identifier for each research study               |
| Source          | Organization or source of the research                  |
| Year            | Year in which the research/report was published         |
| Country/Region  | Geographic region covered by the study                  |
| Industry        | Industry or sector covered                              |
| Sample/Scope    | Population, sample, or scope of the research            |
| Research Focus  | Main topic investigated in the study                    |
| Key Finding     | Major finding reported by the research                  |
| Business Impact | Business outcome or impact associated with the findings |

The dataset covers 5 countries/regions and 6 industries.

🛠️ Excel Tools & Features Used

The following Excel features were used to build the project:

* Data Cleaning & Formatting
* Excel Tables
* PivotTables
* Pivot Charts
* Slicers
